-- =============================================================================================
-- BizApps Accounting v0.24.x -- Metadata_Sync (one per release, generated by the build engineer)
-- =============================================================================================
-- Generated by `mj sync push --dir metadata --ci --exclude scheduled-jobs` (MJ CLI 6.1.6) against a
-- database built from migrations ONLY: MJ core v6.1.6, bizapps-common 5.55.0, bizapps-tasks
-- 1.10.0, then this app's migrations at `next`. Push result: 28 created, 67 updated, 156
-- unchanged, 0 errors.
--
-- CREATED: Finance Exception Types ERP_POSTING_REJECTED, PROVIDER_REFUND_NOT_BOOKED,
-- PROVIDER_CHARGE_MISMATCH, PROVIDER_PAYMENT_ORDER_DUPLICATE and SUBSCRIPTION_TERM_LENGTH; GL
-- Account Role Gift Card Liability; the accounting API scopes (accounting, accounting:read,
-- accounting:write, accounting:post) and their three MJAPI application scopes; eleven
-- authorizations (BooksClosedThroughDate.Set, JournalEntryBatches.Operate, the per-type
-- FinanceExceptions.ClearType.* rights, ClearUnattributed, EscalatedCreator, ClearEscalated) with
-- two Finance grants; the Finance Exceptions Cleared and Journal Entries Held Back By Posting Start
-- Date queries with their fields and entities.
--
-- UPDATED: form categories on 60 entity fields; descriptions on the Cost of Goods Sold, Deferred
-- Revenue and Inventory GL account roles, the Clear Finance Exception remote operation and the
-- FinanceExceptions.Clear authorization; the action category of Build Journal Entry Batches and
-- Run ERP Sync. None reverts a migration.
--
-- NOT INCLUDED, as in 0.17 and 0.20: metadata/scheduled-jobs (the nightly Order & Payment posting
-- and monthly subscription recognition jobs are declared Active -- seeding them switches on ERP
-- posting on every host, which needs its own decision). The ML bench now lives in demo-data/.
--
-- TRANSFORMS: `EXEC [__mj]` -> `EXEC [${mjSchema}]`, `EXEC [__mj_BizAppsAccounting]` ->
-- `EXEC [${flyway:defaultSchema}]`; string values are untouched. Every create is guarded on ID OR
-- the table's unique key, and parents (query category, query, authorization, role, API scope, API
-- application) are re-resolved on the host by name, so a host that ran `mj sync push` is not
-- broken. Idempotent.
-- =============================================================================================
